Per Company Common Stock outstanding, the Merger Consideration consists of (A) one share of Parent Common Stock (the Share Consideration), (B) $50.00 in cash (the Cash Consideration), and (C) one New CVR, with fractional shares settled in cash under Section 2.08.
Exchange Ratio: 1 share of Parent Common Stock per Company Common Stock; Cash Consideration: $50.00 per share; New CVR: 1 New CVR per share; Other forms of consideration include cash in lieu of fractional shares, dividends or other distributions payable with respect to the Share Consideration, New CVR Certificates representing the New CVRs, and Unvested Equity Award CVR Consideration under Section 2.06(e) (which may be New CVR or Milestone Payment or no additional consideration depending on vesting).
Each Company Common Stock share outstanding immediately prior to the Merger Effective Time shall be converted into the right to receive (A) one (the "Exchange Ratio") share of Parent Common Stock (the "Share Consideration"), subject to Section 2.08 with respect to fractional shares, (B) $50.00 in cash without interest (the "Cash Consideration") and (C) one contingent value right (a "New CVR") issued by Parent subject to and in accordance with the New CVR Agreement (the consideration contemplated by subclauses (A), (B) and (C) together, the "Merger Consideration");
